---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import { siteConfig } from '../site.config'

// Deliberately claims no WCAG conformance level: only list commitments the
// test suite (axe, keyboard and reduced-motion e2e) actually backs up.
---

<Legal
    title="Accessibility"
    description={`How ${siteConfig.name} approaches accessibility, what we know falls short, and how to tell us.`}
>
    <p>
        We want {siteConfig.name} to work for as many people as possible.
        Accessibility is a continual process and there is always more work to
        do, so this page says what we aim for and where we know we fall short.
    </p>

    <h2>Our approach</h2>
    <p>
        We build to
        <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/"
            >WCAG 2.2</a
        >
        as our guideline and check pages automatically with axe on every change.
        We don't claim full conformance at any level: automated checks find only
        part of the problems.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Use semantic HTML, with ARIA only where it's needed.</li>
        <li>Size text relatively, so browser zoom and font settings work.</li>
        <li>Make everything usable with a keyboard, with visible focus.</li>
        <li>Provide a "skip to content" link.</li>
        <li>
            Respect your <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> and
            <code>prefers-color-scheme</code> settings, and offer a manual
            light, dark or system theme switch.
        </li>
        <li>Keep text contrast sufficient in both light and dark themes.</li>
        <li>Keep core content available without JavaScript.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Content written by editors, and third-party content they embed, may
            not meet accessibility standards. We fix problems we're told about.
        </li>
        <li>
            The editing (admin) area is a separate product with its own
            accessibility, and isn't covered by the checks above.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Feedback</h2>
    <p>
        If something here is hard to use, tell us at
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}
            >{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a
        >
        {
            siteConfig.feedbackUrl && (
                <>
                    {' '}
                    or <a href={siteConfig.feedbackUrl}>in public</a>
                </>
            )
        }. We take these reports seriously and will do our best to address
        them.
    </p>
</Legal>
